      "is_best": false,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Probably the Ethernet buffers or DMA descriptors are not placed properly in the linker script configuration, on H7 they should be placed in a proper memory region like RAM_D1 (0X2400000), if they are placed in DTCRAM at 0x20000000 on the other hand, the DMA won’t be able to access them. Or the pins are not configured properly.</p><p>Since you are using the Nucleo-H723ZG board, you can try <a href=\"https://mongoose.ws/wizard/#/output?board=h723&amp;ide=CubeIDE&amp;rtos=baremetal&amp;file=README.md\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow ugc\" target=\"_blank\">this example</a> based on the <a href=\"https://mongoose.ws\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow ugc\" target=\"_blank\">Mongoose networking library</a> to rule out any other hardware issues and compare the pin setup to yours from the IOC file. It also comes with a much simpler TCP/IP stack and it’s proven to work, so you shouldn’t lose any more time debugging the low-level driver area. To download the project, just open that URL, go to the `Settings` tab, select a directory on your local machine and then click the `Generate C/C++ Code` blue button in the upper right corner of the page.</p></div>"
    },
    {
      "is_best": false,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Thanks for the suggestion. I have already verified the linker script and memory placement.RX descriptors are placed in <code>.RxDescripSection</code> mapped to <strong>RAM_D2 (0x30000000)</strong>.TX descriptors are placed in <code>.TxDescripSection</code> mapped to <strong>RAM_D2</strong>.RX pool is placed in <code>.Rx_PoolSection</code> mapped to <strong>RAM_D2</strong>.The descriptors are <strong>not</strong> located in DTCM (0x20000000).The ETH GPIO pins were generated by STM32CubeMX for the NUCLEO-H723ZG (RMII mode), and the PHY initializes successfully with link detected.</p><p>The remaining issue is that the RX DMA descriptor <strong>OWN bit never clears</strong>, so <code>HAL_ETH_ReadData()</code> never processes a received frame. Do you know of any H723-specific issue that could cause the DMA to never release the RX descriptors even though PHY initialization and link-up succeed?</p><p> </p><p>if you solve this problem already worked in this specific board so can you attach you ethernet working code ??</p></div>"
    },
